From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:20:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GStreamer] Select the YUV matrix from the colorimetry matrix

https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=330299

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

The YUV to RGB matrix and the transfer function of a video frame were
chosen by comparing its whole GstVideoColorimetry with the presets
bt709, bt2020, bt2100-pq and smpte240m. gst_video_colorimetry_matches()
compares range, matrix, transfer and primaries together, so a frame
that differs from a preset in any one field fell back to BT.601:
full-range BT.709, BT.2020 with the bt2020-10 transfer that 10-bit HEVC
signals, HLG, and streams that signal only some of the fields.

Map the matrix field and the transfer field each on their own, in one
place, VideoFrameGStreamer::yuvColorimetry(), which the DMA-BUF, GL
memory and Qualcomm paths all use. The YUV layer buffer takes the
DMABufBuffer color enums as its own, so the DMA-BUF import passes them
through.

* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/VideoFrameGStreamer.cpp:
(WebCore::VideoFrameGStreamer::getDMABuf):
(WebCore::yuvColorSpaceFromMatrix):
(WebCore::VideoFrameGStreamer::yuvColorimetry const):
* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/VideoFrameGStreamer.h:
* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/texmap/coordinated/CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf.cpp:
(WebCore::CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf::importYUV const):
* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/texmap/coordinated/CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferVideo.cpp:
(WebCore::CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferVideo::createBufferIfNeeded):
(WebCore::CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferVideo::createBufferFromGLMemory):
(WebCore::yuvColorSpaceFromVideoInfo): Deleted.
* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/texmap/coordinated/CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferYUV.h:

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
